 (`accessMode !== 'read_write'`) is consistent with the `sourceAccessModeSchema` defined in Story 0.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-review-sonnet.md:247:**Story 4 → Story 5:** `lastCheckpointResult` is preserved through `rehydrating`/`rebuilding` states in both the client (`process-live.ts` `shouldPreserveCheckpointContext`) and the Convex mutation (`platform-store.ts` conditional on `args.lastCheckpointResult === undefined`). This is correctly compositional.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/05-rehydrate-rebuild-and-recovery/sonnet-review.md:97:- Server-side: `publishRecoveryFailure` does not forward `lastCheckpointResult` when writing the failed state to the store. The in-memory store's `upsertProcessEnvironmentState` only updates fields that are passed — since `lastCheckpointResult` is not passed, it is retained in the durable store row. This is correct behavior and consistent with the \\\"latest-only overwrite\\\" pattern established in Story 4.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/05-rehydrate-rebuild-and-recovery/sonnet-review.md:167:- **Prior story regression:** Server test count 101 and client test count 146 are consistent with a 13-test addition over the Story 4 baseline. No prior story regressions detected.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/00-foundation/sonnet-review.md:64:| `tests/service/client/process-response-composer.test.ts` | 1 assertion fix | Adds `environment: null` to expected state shape; required field fallout from `ProcessSurfaceState` extension |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/04-durable-checkpoint-of-artifacts-and-writable-sources/sonnet-review.md:1:# Story 4 Verification Review — Verifier B (claude-sonnet-4-6)\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/e