-foundation.md:132:| `currentAttachmentVisibility` | enum | yes | `available`, `detached`, `unavailable`, `redacted` | Current enrichment visibility |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/00-foundation.md:133:| `entryStatus` | enum | yes | `ready`, `degraded` | Per-entry resolution status |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/00-foundation.md:134:| `degradationReason` | string/null | yes | non-empty when degraded | Bounded degradation reason |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/00-foundation.md:201:- Shared contracts define repository identity, source attachment summaries, source provenance entries, refresh responses, detach responses, and source-management error codes\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/00-foundation.md:204:- Fixtures cover exact duplicate, missing target ref duplicate, project/process scope coexistence, process-scoped shadowing, pending refresh, soft detach, unavailable source, and degraded provenance\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:25:- `lastHydratedAt` and `freshnessReason` visibility\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:41:- Story 2 source metadata visibility\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:5:Allow users to attach GitHub-backed repositories to a project or one process, with durable identity, scope visibility, duplicate protection, and invalid/inaccessible repository rejection.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:29:- Immediate visibility of repository identity and scope after create\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:49:| 1 | What exact browser interaction model should attach, update, refresh, and detach use without creating a separate source-management app? | Extend the existing project shell and process work surface. Project-scoped actions appear in the project source section; process-scoped actions appear in the process materials/source area. Client calls Fastify JSON APIs and renders settled/pending/degraded responses in-place. No standalone source app or live source subscription is added. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:50:| 2 | What exact durable schema should represent source attachments and provenance visibility? | Extend `sourceAttachments` with `repositoryFullName`, freshness fields, refresh progress fields, and soft-detach fields. Add `sourceProvenance` for process-specific provenance with copied immutable source identity. Artifact ownership remains untouched. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:55:| 7 | What exact current-source read algorithm combines scopes and degrades boundedly? | `resolveActiveProcessSources` excludes detached rows, starts from current material refs, pulls in process-scoped siblings when they shadow an active project-scoped source, partitions by scope, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, sorts by `updatedAt`, and preserves per-row degraded metadata. |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:95:| Processes | Core architecture | Process-scoped attachments, current-source views, and source provenance appear in the process work surface |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:99:| Archive | Core architecture | Downstream consumer only; Epic 6 provides source provenance that Epic 7 can reference |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:170:├── sourceProvenance.ts                          # NEW: durable source provenance records and process reads\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:174:├── schemas.ts                                   # MODIFIED: source summary fields, source provenance schemas\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:199:└── source-attachment-section.ts                 # MODIFIED: management controls and pending/degraded state display\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:223:| `SourceProvenanceService` | New | Record/read provenance, enrich degraded entries independently | PlatformStore | AC-4.x, AC-5.2 |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:226:| Client source sections | Modified/New | Render management controls, freshness, provenance, detach, degraded states | Shared contracts | AC-1.2, AC-2.x, AC-3.x, AC-4.x, AC-5.x, AC-6.x |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:300:  entryStatus: v.union(v.literal('ready'), v.literal('degraded')),\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:324:- `currentAttachmentVisibility: 'available' | 'detached' | 'unavailable' | 'redacted'`\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:329:`currentAttachmentVisibility: 'redacted'`.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:399:  currentAttachmentVisibility: 'available' | 'detached' | 'unavailable' | 'redacted';\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:400:  entryStatu