 provenance.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:639:        reason: \\\"Added Story 4 API coverage for informing, receiving, and degraded provenance responses.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:645:        reason: \\\"Added Story 4 client coverage for empty and degraded provenance states.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:675:        - \\\"Covered the Story 4 read-only exclusion, degraded entry fallback, empty state, and API rendering paths with automated tests.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:691:      path: \\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/003-implementor.json\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:700:path: /Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/004-verify.json\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:716:      storyId: \\\"04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:719:      id: \\\"04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:723:      - \\\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:726:      - \\\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/003-implementor.json\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:753:        evidence: \\\"`apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts:176-187` catches every non-`UNAUTHENTICATED` failure from `getProcessSourceProvenance` and returns `{ entries: [] }`. `apps/platform/client/features/processes/source-provenance-section.ts:37-42` renders any empty `entries` list as `No source provenance has been recorded for this process yet.` The current client tests only cover a true-empty response and degraded entry rendering (`tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts:11-45`); they do not cover this bootstrap failure path. In production, a 403/404/500 or transient provenance read failure is therefore presented as a real no-provenance process, which violates TC-4.1b's empty-state semantics and the story's anti-shim rule against fake runtime fallbacks.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-