{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts\"","aggregated_output":"import type { SourceAttachmentSummary } from '../../../shared/contracts/index.js';\n\nfunction sortByUpdatedAtDesc<T extends { updatedAt: string }>(items: T[]): T[] {\n  return [...items].sort((left, right) => right.updatedAt.localeCompare(left.updatedAt));\n}\n\nfunction buildShadowKey(\n  sourceAttachment: Pick<SourceAttachmentSummary, 'repositoryFullName' | 'targetRef'>,\n): string {\n  return `${sourceAttachment.repositoryFullName}:${sourceAttachment.targetRef ?? ''}`;\n}\n\nexport function resolveActiveProcessSourceAttachments(args: {\n  sourceAttachments: SourceAttachmentSummary[];\n  processId: string;\n  currentSourceAttachmentIds: string[];\n}): SourceAttachmentSummary[] {\n  const currentSourceAttachmentIds = new Set(args.currentSourceAttachmentIds);\n  const activeAttachments = args.sourceAttachments.filter((sourceAttachment) => {\n    if (sourceAttachment.detachedAt != null) {\n      return false;\n    }\n\n    return (\n      sourceAttachment.attachmentScope === 'project' ||\n      sourceAttachment.processId === args.processId\n    );\n  });\n  const processScopedRows = activeAttachments.filter(\n    (sourceAttachment) => sourceAttachment.processId === args.processId,\n  );\n  const visibleByShadowKey = new Map<string, SourceAttachmentSummary>();\n\n  for (const sourceAttachment of processScopedRows) {\n    if (!currentSourceAttachmentIds.has(sourceAttachment.sourceAttachmentId)) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    visibleByShadowKey.set(buildShadowKey(sourceAttachment), sourceAttachment);\n  }\n\n  for (const sourceAttachment of activeAttachments) {\n    if (\n      sourceAttachment.attachmentScope !== 'project' ||\n      !currentSourceAttachmentIds.has(sourceAttachment.sourceAttachmentId)\n    ) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    const processScopedSibling = processScopedRows.find(\n      (candidate) =>\n        candidate.repositoryFullName === sourceAttachment.repositoryFullName &&\n        candidate.targetRef === sourceAttachment.targetRef,\n    );\n\n    visibleByShadowKey.set(\n      buildShadowKey(sourceAttachment),\n      processScopedSibling ?? sourceAttachment,\n    );\n  }\n\n  return sortByUpdatedAtDesc([...visibleByShadowKey.values()]);\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ve got a concrete repro seam and the likely causes. Ranked hypotheses before I patch:\n\n1. The read models are forwarding durable source rows directly, so unavailable rows keep old `lastHydrated*`, `freshnessReason`, and project-shell resolved-ref snapshots.\n2. The process materials mapper is only gating UI-visible fields at render time, not redacting them in the route payload.\n3. The source refresh sync path normalizes availability state but intentionally leaves historical hydration data on the durable row, which is fine for storage but wrong for read serialization.\n\nPlan:\n1. Add a server-side redaction helper for unavailable source rows that preserves safe identity/scope fields and healthy-row behavior.\n2. Apply it in both the project shell source reader and the process materials current-source mapper, without changing the outer section envelopes.\n3. Update route-backed server tests to prove TC-6.2a on both `GET /api/projects/:projectId` and `GET /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId`, and tighten the mixed-row project test so healthy rows still keep their metadata.\n4. Run the focused story tests, then the configured story gate."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"todo_list","items":[{"text":"Patch project/process source read models to redact unavailable-row hydration metadata while preserving healthy rows and section envelopes","completed":false},{"text":"Add/update route-backed Story 6 tests proving TC-6.2a and mixed healthy/unavailable behavior","completed":false},{"text":"Run focused story tests and the configured story gate","completed":false}]}}
