{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"agent_message","text":"Unavailable-source redaction now happens at the server read-model seam, so real project-shell and process work-surface payloads keep safe identity/scope fields but stop serializing stale hydration metadata or resolved-ref snapshots for unavailable rows. I added the shared logic in [source-read-models.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-read-models.ts), then wired it into [source-summary.builder.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/projects/summary/source-summary.builder.ts) and [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts). Healthy rows still preserve their existing metadata, and the outer section envelopes are unchanged.\n\nTC-6.2a is now proven through actual route/read behavior in [projects-api.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts) and [process-work-surface-api.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts). The mixed project-shell case also now asserts that healthy rows stay intact while the unavailable row is bounded/redacted.\n\nVerification passed:\n- `corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts`\n- `corepack pnpm run green-verify`\n\nI left the unrelated existing worktree changes untouched."}}
